        "answer": "*Spider-Man: Brand New Day* is an MCU film released in the United States on July 31, 2026, as part of Phase Six. It premiered at the Dolby Theatre in Hollywood, Los Angeles, on July 27, 2026.\n\n**Performance and Reception**\nThe film received largely positive reviews from critics, who praised Tom Holland's performance, the action sequences, and the story for being more mature and character-driven than previous MCU Spider-Man films. It has been a major commercial success, grossing $2.333 billion worldwide. It holds the titles of the highest-grossing Spider-Man film, the highest-grossing film of 2026, and the fourth-highest grossing film of all time. Additionally, it was nominated for Most Anticipated Film at the 9th Astra Midseason Movie Awards.\n\n**Production and Content**\n*   **Creative Direction:** Kevin Feige stated that the film centers on \"classic elements\" of Spider-Man and features a pairing between Spider-Man and The Punisher to focus on \"street-level crime as opposed to world-ending events.\" \n*   **Development:** Tom Holland noted that new scenes were filmed to add \"more humor\" and layer in a villain plotline. The film also features a plot point involving Spider-Man mutating and gaining new powers.\n*   **The Title:** The title refers to a \"Brand New Day\" comic book storyline that explores a reset for Spider-Man following the 2007\u20132008 \"One More Day\" storyline. While there was speculation about whether the film would adapt specific elements from the comics\u2014such as Peter Parker making a deal with Mephisto to resurrect Aunt May\u2014commentators noted that the film could follow a similar storyline without undoing character growth.\n\n**Production Challenges**\nAccording to Tom Holland, an early cut of the film shown at test screenings \"took notes from random people\" and \"totally didn't work,\" leading to a negative reaction.",
